Need design.

Item 1: when 0 musics, show "Nenhuma música tem essa sequência" instead of "Encontrei essas músicas". Also the "Encontrei essas músicas" button in left panel appears (showSearchResultsCount true) even when 0; user says screen shows "Encontrei essas musicas" and nothing below. That is the right panel h4 `esfigeSpeech`, and left button. We should handle both:
- On success, if `data.length === 0`: set `vm.esfigeSpeech = "Nenhuma música tem essa sequência."`, `vm.showSearchResultsCount = false` (hide the jump button), maybe `vm.semResultados = true`.
- Else normal.

Item 2: show "mostrando 100 de 216" near results when total > 100. Need know total. For a catalog sequence, `vm.minhaSequencia.total_musicas` is the unfiltered count. For new sequence selected after creation, mapped from GET /sequencias includes total. For genre filter, total_musicas unfiltered. Could compute filtered total? no. Could display "mostrando 100 de 216" only when no filter; when filter active, perhaps "mostrando 100 (filtro: Rock)"? The user didn't mention genre. But we should avoid misleading. Options:

A) Add `vm.totalResultados` set from `vm.minhaSequencia.total_musicas` only when no genre filter, else null. Template shows note when `musics.length < totalResultados` maybe. But for filtered, hide. Requirement "quando o total passar de 100 mostra..." satisfied for default.

B) Better: have backend include total in response? Let's evaluate whether small. `/similares?sequencia=` currently returns `json.dumps(get_pagina(out, pagina_tag))`. Adding total would break API shape (client expects array) and tests. Not good.

C) Use a separate request to compute filtered total? No.

D) Frontend loads all pages progressively in background to count? No.

A is sensible, but if user selects genre with 216 total and gets 100 results, no note, despite "total > 100". But actual filtered total could be <100 or >100 unknown. Hiding is honest. Could show "mostrando 100 (total sem filtro: 216)"? That's ugly. Better: show total note only when no filter; when filter active, maybe "mostrando 100 (filtro de gênero)" if `musics.length === 100`? Not exact total.

Wait, maybe `vm.minhaSequencia.total_musicas` is per sequence and all songs regardless genre. Could still label "mostrando 100 de 216 no catálogo" but filter makes it wrong. Since the user didn't ask about filter, just implement for unfiltered and document in code. But user might test with filter and see no note. That's acceptable perhaps.

Alternatively, could have the backend `/similares` response include total via header `X-Total-Count` while keeping body array, and Angular reads headers. That's a small backend change, but changing API headers is less breaking and tests can ignore. But user says two screen adjustments; adding header might be overkill and extra code. Also CORS? same origin. Angular `$http` response has headers. But we'd need Flask `Response` with header instead of tuple; every endpoint uses json.dumps string intentionally. Could return `app.response_class(json.dumps(...), headers={'X-Total-Count': str(len(out))})` — changes content type maybe. That's a real API change. Not asked. Avoid.

Could compute total by making a second GET for `pagina=2`? Only tells if there are more, not total. Could fetch all pages for count then only display first page; heavy but for 216 it's 3 requests. But no, unnecessary.

Maybe use the catalog total and show only if no genre filter. I'll implement with a dedicated `vm.totalMusicas` and `vm.mostrandoPaginado` flag.

